      "title": "Graph detanglement — the practice, not the migration",
      "description": "Drive a tangled graph toward a clean partition, so a sub-graph can be split off when it grows too large or when a business reason separates it. The staged practice — declare in place, detangle, isolate, extract — with the seventeen moves that were measured rather than argued, and the failures each one cost.",
